{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"mexican murals\" \"mexican muralism\") (+ \"all social groups\" \"common people\" masses) (+ messages public art))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_243665182#8_552716544","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q165","rank":2,"snippet":"what I mean, I want them to understand.\" Summary of Mexican Muralism Key Ideas & Accomplishments Overview of Mexican Muralism Key Artists José Clemente Orozco Do Not Miss Important Art and Artists of Mexican Muralism The Creation (1922) Los Danzantes de Chalma (1922) The Banquet of the Rich (1923-24) Useful Resources on Mexican Muralism Books scholarly/biographical Share Do more \" , \"segment\": \"Overview of Mexican Muralism Saying, \\\"The role of the artist is that of a soldier in a revolution,\\\" Diego Rivera pioneered <cover>Mexican Muralism. He said his portrayals of the revolutionary Zapata and his followers were meant to make \"the masses the hero of monumental art.\" </cover>Beginnings and Development Concepts, Trends, & Related Topics Later Developments and Legacy Key Artists Diego Rivera Quick view Read more Diego Rivera was the principal actor in the Mexican Muralism movement and one of Mexico's greatest artists. His large-scale fresco cycles tell the histories of labor, industry, society, and other themes. José Clemente Orozco Quick view Read more José Clemente Orozco was a Mexican Muralist, a social realist painter who is best known for his large-scale expansive works depicting human toil, Mexican politics, and the advent ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_243665182#7_552714236","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
